Keep the seat's structure — it is right — and harden three things.

1. The magic height. The menu measures 188x213, not 219, at both 390 and 1440 (label 40px + five 34px items + gaps + 5px padding; B.columns is five: To do, In progress, Review, Waiting, Done). 219 is a safe over-estimate today, but it rots the moment a lane is added or removed. Derive it instead of typing it: `const MH = 46 + 35 * B.columns.length;` (=221 for five), and use the same constant in the flip test and the flip offset.

2. Two missing clamps. The flip branch can push `top` negative on a short viewport, and neither branch is bounded below. Bound both ends:
```js
if (what === "menu") {
  const card = act.closest(".card");
  const box = act.getBoundingClientRect();
  /* Never measure the suite host: `.app` is `display: contents` and its
     rect is all zeros. The menu's containing block is `.floor`. */
  const frame = document.querySelector(".floor").getBoundingClientRect();
  const MW = 200, MH = 46 + 35 * B.columns.length;
  let top = box.bottom + MH > innerHeight
    ? box.top - frame.top - MH - 6
    : box.bottom - frame.top + 6;
  top = Math.max(8, Math.min(top, innerHeight - frame.top - MH - 8));
  const left = Math.max(8, Math.min(box.left - frame.left, innerWidth - frame.left - MW));
  menuAt = "left:" + Math.round(left) + "px;top:" + Math.round(top) + "px";
  ...
}
```

3. Best of all, stop guessing the height. The menu exists immediately after `mount()`. Correct it there, before the focus call, and the constant stops being load-bearing:
```js
mount();
const m = document.querySelector(".cardMenu");
if (m) {
  const r = m.getBoundingClientRect();
  const dy = Math.min(0, innerHeight - 8 - r.bottom);
  const dx = Math.min(0, innerWidth - 8 - r.right);
  if (dy || dx) {
    menuAt = "left:" + Math.round(parseFloat(m.style.left) + dx) +
             "px;top:" + Math.round(parseFloat(m.style.top) + dy) + "px";
    m.setAttribute("style", menuAt);
  }
}
```

The seat's closing rule is the real lesson and should go in as a comment: never clamp against a rect that can be zero — a `display: contents` ancestor must not be allowed to decide where a popover lands. Worth a grep for the same shape elsewhere; `__SUITE.host(...)` + `getBoundingClientRect` is the signature.

One thing the seat's fix does not cover: at ≤720 the dock/capsule sits at the foot of the floor, and clamping to `innerHeight` can drop the menu underneath it. Clamp to the dock's top when the dock is on screen, not to the window.

Bind at construction, not by delegation, and let `nearest` do the work.

In `behindBlock` (src/timeline.js:1089), give the details node an `on` map — the `h()` builder already supports one (src/timeline.js:41: `if (key === "on") { for (var evt in value) el.addEventListener(evt, value[evt]); }`), and the block is rebuilt on every render so the handler travels with it:

    h("details.b-behindDetails", {
      on: { toggle: function (event) {
        var d = event.currentTarget;
        if (!d.open) return;
        var rows = d.querySelectorAll(".b-behindRow");
        if (rows.length) rows[rows.length - 1].scrollIntoView({ block: "nearest" });
      } },
    }, [ h("summary.b-behindSummary", {}, head), rowsNode ])

Three constraints on the implementation:
- Do NOT delegate on `root`. `toggle` has `bubbles: false` (measured on this element: capture 1, bubble 0), so `root.addEventListener("toggle", …)` never fires. If delegation is wanted for consistency with the rest of the file, it must be capture-phase: `root.addEventListener("toggle", handler, true)`.
- Keep `block: "nearest"` and add nothing else. `nearest` is a no-op wherever the rows already fit (measured: 390×844, 768×1024, 1280×900 all unchanged), and it leaves the summary on screen for free at 1440 and 1920 — verified. `block: "end"` or a `scrollTop` assignment would scroll on every open including the ones that are already correct, and would drag the summary toward the sheet's top edge.
- No `behavior: "smooth"`. Instant matches the only existing precedent in the product, `land()` at src/timeline.js:1894, and keeps the motion gate out of it.
- Guard on `d.open` so closing never scrolls. Nothing else needs to change: the `data-past="listed"` and `print` branches render `.b-behindHead` with no `<details>` at all, so they take no handler.
